# EWM Warehouse Inbound Delivery (A2X, OData V4) — GR test harness
# Extension: REST Client (humao.rest-client)
# Fill values in .env (see ewm-ibd-gr.env.example). Run requests top-to-bottom.
#
# Full GR    = POST PostGoodsReceipt on the header with empty body.
# Partial GR = PATCH item qty first, then POST the action (best: one $batch changeset).
# HU GR      = not a released public action — see notes at bottom.

@base = https://{{$dotenv HOST}}/sap/opu/odata4/sap/api_warehouseinbounddelivery/srvd_a2x/sap/warehouseinbounddelivery/0001
@client = {{$dotenv SAP_CLIENT}}
@auth = Basic {{$dotenv BASIC_AUTH_B64}}
@ibd = {{$dotenv IBD_NUMBER}}

### 0. Service document — sanity check auth/reachability
GET {{base}}/?sap-client={{client}}
Authorization: {{auth}}
Accept: application/json

### 1. $metadata — COPY the real action name + editable qty property from here
GET {{base}}/$metadata?sap-client={{client}}
Authorization: {{auth}}
Accept: application/xml

### 2. List open inbound deliveries (find one to test)
GET {{base}}/WarehouseInboundDelivery?sap-client={{client}}&$top=20&$orderby=WarehouseInboundDelivery desc
Authorization: {{auth}}
Accept: application/json

### 3. Read one delivery + its items (expand)
GET {{base}}/WarehouseInboundDelivery('{{ibd}}')?sap-client={{client}}&$expand=_Item
Authorization: {{auth}}
Accept: application/json

### 4. Fetch CSRF token + session cookies (reuse on every write below)
# @name csrf
GET {{base}}/WarehouseInboundDelivery('{{ibd}}')?sap-client={{client}}
Authorization: {{auth}}
Accept: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: Fetch

@token = {{csrf.response.headers.x-csrf-token}}
@cookie = {{csrf.response.headers.set-cookie}}

### 5a. FULL GR — bound action on the header, empty body
# Replace SAP__self.PostGoodsReceipt with the exact qualified name from step 1 if different.
POST {{base}}/WarehouseInboundDelivery('{{ibd}}')/SAP__self.PostGoodsReceipt?sap-client={{client}}
Authorization: {{auth}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{token}}
Cookie: {{cookie}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{}

### 5b. PARTIAL GR — step 1: PATCH the item's received/actual qty
# Confirm the item key segment and the PATCHable qty property name from step 1 metadata.
PATCH {{base}}/WarehouseInboundDeliveryItem(WarehouseInboundDelivery='{{ibd}}',WarehouseInboundDeliveryItem='10')?sap-client={{client}}
Authorization: {{auth}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{token}}
Cookie: {{cookie}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "QuantityToPost": "5",
  "QuantityToPostUnit": "KG"
}

### 5c. PARTIAL GR — step 2: post the action (header)
POST {{base}}/WarehouseInboundDelivery('{{ibd}}')/SAP__self.PostGoodsReceipt?sap-client={{client}}
Authorization: {{auth}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{token}}
Cookie: {{cookie}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{}

### 6. RELIABLE PARTIAL — PATCH + action in ONE $batch changeset (atomic, ordered)
# Use this if 5b/5c are rejected outside a batch (common for A2X V4).
POST {{base}}/$batch?sap-client={{client}}
Authorization: {{auth}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{token}}
Cookie: {{cookie}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "requests": [
    {
      "id": "1",
      "method": "PATCH",
      "url": "WarehouseInboundDeliveryItem(WarehouseInboundDelivery='{{ibd}}',WarehouseInboundDeliveryItem='10')",
      "headers": { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
      "body": { "QuantityToPost": "5", "QuantityToPostUnit": "KG" }
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "dependsOn": ["1"],
      "method": "POST",
      "url": "WarehouseInboundDelivery('{{ibd}}')/SAP__self.PostGoodsReceipt",
      "headers": { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
      "body": {}
    }
  ]
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HU-BASED GR — no released public action on the inbound delivery.
# Options:
#   (a) Resolve the HU -> its delivery items, PATCH those items, then post (5b/5c or 6).
#   (b) Custom RAP/SOAP wrapper over /SCWM/CL_API_FACTORY_DELIVERY ->
#       /SCWM/IF_API_DELIVERY_IBD (released ABAP API, supports HU-level GR).
# Property names above (QuantityToPost / item key) are PLACEHOLDERS — confirm from step 1.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
